Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd, yttrium: allow 192 combined texture slots in a shader

A Direct3D 10 or 11 shader names a texture and a sampler state apart. The
frontend gives every pair that a shader uses one combined slot, and a typed
buffer load takes a slot from the same range. The range had 32 slots, the
value of PIPE_MAX_SAMPLERS. A pixel shader that needed more was replaced by
one that writes zero, so its draws left the render target black. Wine's
test_high_resource_count needs 150 slots.

The range has PIPE_MAX_SHADER_SAMPLER_SLOTS entries now, 192. The 32 came
from five places, and each of them changes:

- The frontend's slot table and the sampler binding map it hands to the
  driver. The masks of the map are word arrays.
- TGSI. ureg, tgsi_scan and tgsi_to_nir declare and index sampler and
  sampler-view registers up to the new limit. The 32-bit masks of
  tgsi_shader_info and the bitsets of shader_info keep their size and have
  no bit for a higher register.
- nir_to_spirv, whose table of sampler variables is indexed by the slot.
- The Yttrium shader state. Its slot masks are struct
  yttrium_sampler_slot_mask, and the slots a shader uses are read from its
  tokens and from its sampler variables, not from shader_info alone.
- The Yttrium pipeline. A pipeline holds up to 192 sampled images. The
  descriptor bindings of the slots below 32 are unchanged, and the slots
  from 32 up get a second binding range behind the storage images, so a
  shader that fits the old range compiles to the same SPIR-V as before.

Three per-draw costs would have grown with the arrays, so they are bounded
by the number of sampled bindings in use: the pipeline key is cleared and
compared up to that number, a deferred draw record is cleared up to it, and
the search for a sampler object stops at it.

A shader that needs more than 192 slots still gets the zero shader and the
same log line, which now names 192.

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/nir/tgsi_to_nir.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/nir/tgsi_to_nir.c
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/nir/tgsi_to_nir.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/nir/tgsi_to_nir.c
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ struct ttn_compile {
 
    nir_variable **inputs;
    nir_variable **outputs;
-   nir_variable *samplers[PIPE_MAX_SAMPLERS];
+   nir_variable *samplers[PIPE_MAX_SHADER_SAMPLER_SLOTS];
    nir_variable *images[PIPE_MAX_SHADER_IMAGES];
    nir_variable *ssbo[PIPE_MAX_SHADER_BUFFERS];
    uint32_t ubo_sizes[PIPE_MAX_CONSTANT_BUFFERS];
@@ -1595,11 +1595,16 @@ get_sampler_var(struct ttn_compile *c, int binding,
       c->samplers[binding] = var;
       c->num_samplers = MAX2(c->num_samplers, binding + 1);
 
-      /* Record textures used */
-      BITSET_SET(c->build.shader->info.textures_used, binding);
-      if (op == nir_texop_txf || op == nir_texop_txf_ms)
-         BITSET_SET(c->build.shader->info.textures_used_by_txf, binding);
-      BITSET_SET(c->build.shader->info.samplers_used, binding);
+      /* Record textures used.  shader_info has 128 texture bits and 32
+       * sampler bits; a binding above them is found through its variable.
+       */
+      if (binding < 128) {
+         BITSET_SET(c->build.shader->info.textures_used, binding);
+         if (op == nir_texop_txf || op == nir_texop_txf_ms)
+            BITSET_SET(c->build.shader->info.textures_used_by_txf, binding);
+      }
+      if (binding < 32)
+         BITSET_SET(c->build.shader->info.samplers_used, binding);
    }
 
    return var;
